Package: forkingpaths
Type: Package
Title: A p-Hacking Roguelike for the R Console
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tudor", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "chickengalactica@gmail.com")
Description: A turn-based roguelike for bored statisticians. Each study
    starts with a dataset and a preregistered analysis. Spend your
    researcher degrees of freedom on outlier exclusion, covariates,
    outcome switching, subgroups and optional stopping until p < alpha,
    then face Reviewer 2 and the replication crisis. Survive three years
    with your credibility intact and earn tenure. Then find out how many
    of your findings were real.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    graphics,
    grDevices,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
